{% doc %}
  The mount point Swiper's Pagination module renders into.

  ## What this replaces

  A hand-written list of `<button data-indicator>` dots, and a
  `<carousel-pagination>` custom element backed by
  `assets/carousel-pagination.js` that measured the track at runtime to compute
  a page count for the numbers and the progress bar.

  All of it is one empty element now. Swiper's Pagination module already knows
  the slide count, the pages, the active index and the click targets, and it
  renders bullets, a fraction or a progress bar into whatever element it is
  given. The type comes from `data-options`.

  **`assets/carousel-pagination.js` is deleted** along with its import map entry
  — nothing references it any more.

  ## Why the element is empty

  Liquid cannot know how many slides fit in the viewport, so it cannot know how
  many pages there are. The old dots markup guessed one dot per slide and relied
  on the component to hide the extras. Letting Swiper render them means the
  count is right the first time rather than corrected after a measurement.

  `controls` is not handled here — it is `carousel-controls.liquid`, because it
  carries navigation as well and Swiper has no pagination type for it.

  @param {string} [style] - dots | numbers | progress. Anything else, including
    nothing, renders no pagination.

  @example
    {% render 'carousel-pagination', style: 'dots' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign style = style | default: 'none'

  case style
    when 'dots'
      assign class = 'carousel-shell__dots'
    when 'numbers'
      assign class = 'carousel-shell__counter'
    when 'progress'
      assign class = 'carousel-shell__progress'
    else
      assign class = blank
  endcase
-%}

{%- if class != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    `aria-hidden` on the non-interactive types because the position is already
    announced through the carousel's own `role="status"` region. Bullets are
    clickable controls, so they stay reachable; a fraction and a bar are
    decoration, and a second announcement of the same change is noise.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="{{ class }}"
    data-ref="pagination"
    {% unless style == 'dots' %}aria-hidden="true"{% endunless %}
  ></div>
{%- endif -%}
